  "details": "Networking.LocalPlayer should not be null.\nFor example, the following process does not usually cause problems while playing with the VRChat client.\nHowever, an exception to Networking.LocalPlayer is raised when exiting the instance, which leaves an error log.\nThis means that projects that make heavy use of Networking.LocalPlayer will have their logs filled with a large number of \"unimportant\" critical errors when debugging.\nprivate void Update ()\n{\n    var selfPosition = NetWorking.LocalPlayer.GetPosition();\n    ...\n}\npublic override void OnPlayerLeft(VRCPlayerApi player)\n{\n    var leftPlayerName = player.displayName;\n    ...\n}\nAs a workaround, I can run Utilities.IsValid(Networking.LocalPlayer) at all points, but in an action-packed game world, I want to shave off even one line of functionality to improve performance.\nIdeally, Networking.LocalPlayer should remain in existence until all UDON scripts for that instance have been created and destroyed.\nApproximate canny : https://vrchat.canny.io/vrchat-udon-closed-alpha-bugs/p/vrcplayerapiplayerid-may-returns-1-in-onplayerleft",
